4. LICENSE KEY USAGE

Medio can be installed and used free of charge. Features marked Premium in
the Software require the purchase of a Premium license key.

A Premium license key is personal to one person:

  - A key may be used on up to 3 computers at the same time. You can
    release a computer in Arctisoft Studio Hub to use the license on
    another one. A computer that has not used the license for 45 days is
    released automatically.
  - Sharing, publishing or distributing your license key is prohibited.
  - A license may be passed on only as a whole, using the transfer
    function in Arctisoft Studio Hub. After a transfer you may no longer
    use it.
  - Keys that are misused or obtained by fraud may be deactivated.

The computers using a license are recorded solely to apply these limits,
not to track individual user activity. The License Agreement in Arctisoft
Studio Hub states the complete terms.


5. DATA HANDLING

Medio stores workspace state, queues, device statistics, and device history
locally. An Arctisoft account is optional for the standalone application.

When signed in, account services store authentication information including
your account email, product license records, and the Medio preferences you
choose to synchronize. Shared account services also manage your profile
image if you upload one through Arctisoft Studio Hub.

If history tracking is enabled while signed in, recent history is stored
in your account. Records can include URLs, titles, dates, outcomes, formats,
output file paths, and measured media properties. Output paths may contain
personal folder names. Cloud history retains a bounded set of recent records;
device history and exported records are separate from that account history.

Medio's device usage totals are not uploaded as account usage counters.
Downloaded media, file contents, browser passwords, and activity outside
Medio are not uploaded as account history. Payment card information is
handled by the payment provider rather than stored by Medio.

Use Settings > Privacy & Sync to control history tracking and synchronized
preferences. History provides record removal, clearing, and export actions.
Account management, including account deletion, is available through
Arctisoft Studio Hub. Uninstalling Medio preserves your personal files and
local application data; it does not delete an Arctisoft account.


